MewStage vendor patch allocation/0006 (third_party/NOTICE): a dashed stroke allocates nothing per draw.
NvgStrokeHelper (linked into the MewStage backend) built a new List<DashSegment> per dashed stroke and a new
PathGeometry per dashed line / rect / ellipse / rounded rect; the flattened segments now go into a per-thread list,
line / rect / ellipse paths into a per-thread scratch path, and rounded-rect paths are cached per thread by their
geometry (bounded, cleared when full). A re-recorded frame of a dashed line + rect + rounded rect + ellipse then
costs the same as the frame drawn with a solid pen, and a replayed frame is 0 B. Behaviour unchanged.

